## Document-by-Document Findings

| Document | Content Type | Financial Data Present? |
|---|---|---|
| #1 — Sep 30, 2024 Statutory Results PDF | Financial statements (IGAAP) | **Yes** — source of all values above |
| #2 — Compliance Officer (Reg. 6(1)) disclosure | Administrative/regulatory | No — purely names/designation details |
| #3 — RTA (Reg. 7(1)) disclosure | Administrative/regulatory | No — registrar & transfer agent details only |
| #4 — Investor Grievance Report | Regulatory tracking report | No — grievance counts, not financials |
| #5 — Investor relations landing page | Navigation index | No — links only to statutory PDFs; no separate H1FY25 investor deck surfaced |

## Line Items Not Available in This Filing

The following requested line items could **not be populated**, as they are genuinely not disclosed in the statutory PDF reviewed (document #1), and per the sourcing rules, no estimate was substituted:

- **Total GWP** and **Retail health GWP** — the "Gross Premium Written" row in the source table returned internally inconsistent OCR'd digit sequences that do not reconcile against NWP/NEP in the same filing, indicating scan/OCR corruption on that specific line — left blank rather than guessed.
- **Claims ratio, Expense ratio, Commission ratio, Combined ratio, Solvency ratio** (IGAAP) — the "Analytical Ratios" section in this filing covers debt-equity, current ratio, EoM ratio, operating margin, net earning ratio, and GDPI growth rate, but does **not** separately break out these underwriting ratios.
- **Retail health market share** — not disclosed in a statutory quarterly filing of this type.
- **PAT (IFRS)** and **Claims/Expense ratio (IFRS)** — not applicable; Niva Bupa reports exclusively under IGAAP per IRDAI regulations, so no IFRS-basis figures exist in this document set.

## Key Observations

**PAT turned negative in H1FY25**, with a reported net loss of ₹5.80 crore, largely driven by a ₹162.05 crore Expense of Management (EoM) excess-over-allowable-limit charge transferred from the Revenue Account to the P&L Account for the six-month period (per Note 6 of the filing). This is a material regulatory/one-off item that should be flagged when benchmarking against peers (e.g., Star Health) or against any investor-deck PAT figure that may treat this EoM forbearance differently.

**Net worth grew modestly**, from ₹2,049.59 crore at FY24 year-end (March 31, 2024) to ₹2,064.55 crore at September 30, 2024 — an increase of roughly **0.7%** over the half-year. This growth was largely supported by ESOP-related equity infusion (~₹20.81 crore from share capital proceeds), which offset the reported net loss.

**AUM (proxied as Investments–Shareholders + Investments–Policyholders) expanded meaningfully**, rising from ₹5,458.23 crore at FY24-end to ₹5,965.21 crore at September 30, 2024 — an increase of approximately **9.3%** in six months. This signals continued float/reserve accumulation even as the P&L reported a loss for the period.

**Investment yield improved year-on-year**, reaching 4.83% (with unrealised gains, YTD) for H1FY25 versus 3.99% for the equivalent H1FY24 YTD period — an improvement of roughly **84 basis points**.

## Recommendation for Completing the Dataset

To fill the remaining blank cells — **Total GWP, Retail health GWP, Claims/Expense/Commission/Combined/Solvency ratios, Retail health market share, and IFRS PAT** — the following additional sources should be pursued:

1. **Niva Bupa's Investor Presentation for H1FY25** — typically released alongside statutory results but distinct from the statutory PDF, and usually where headline GWP, PAT, and underwriting ratios are disclosed in an investor-friendly format.
2. **The IRDAI NL-1 (Revenue Account) and NL-2 return set** filed separately on the IRDAI portal or the company's public-disclosures page — these carry granular underwriting ratios (claims, expense, commission, combined ratios) in a standardized regulatory format not present in the statutory results PDF reviewed here.

If you'd like, I can proceed to search for and extract data from either of these two supplementary sources to complete the table.</ans>
